--- !u!114 &914785268
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 914785267}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 83c90e794281e6c45a7e3be79a668332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InteriorDialogueManager
  minigameScene: EmailSwiper
  returnScene: WorldMap
  introLines:
  - speaker: NPC
    text: Hey, come in! I was just about to call you.
  - speaker: Player
    text: What's up, Tony? You look stressed.
  - speaker: NPC
    text: The shop computer keeps getting pop-ups saying it's infected with a virus!
  - speaker: Player
    text: "Let me guess \u2014 they want you to call a number and give remote access?"
  - speaker: NPC
    text: Exactly! They say they'll fix it for free. Seems fishy to me.
  - speaker: Player
    text: Good instinct. That's a tech support scam. Never give access to someone
      who contacts you first.
  - speaker: NPC
    text: Can you check my inbox? There are some suspicious emails in there too.
  - speaker: Player
    text: Absolutely. Let's sort through them together.
  winLines:
  - speaker: NPC
    text: Wow, you spotted every single one! That's impressive.
  - speaker: Player
    text: Once you know the patterns, they're not hard to catch.
  - speaker: NPC
    text: The fake sender addresses were a dead giveaway, right?
  - speaker: Player
    text: Exactly. Real businesses never ask for login info by email.
  - speaker: NPC
    text: I'm sharing this with my staff. Thanks a million!
  loseLines:
  - speaker: NPC
    text: Hmm, a couple of those tripped you up, eh?
  - speaker: Player
    text: They were pretty convincing. Want me to try again?
  - speaker: NPC
    text: Please! I need this place protected.
